Rust-Orbital Twang

Ingredients: CLASSIC COUNTRY / HILLBILLY + CELESTIAL, SPACE & ORBITAL + Vibraphone
Creative Catalyst: Born at an illegal rooftop rave on the rusted water-towers of a flooded megacity in 2091.

High-rig twang collides with zero-G acoustics: imagine a high-lonesome Grand Ole Opry vocal bouncing off the ice-crust of Jupiter’s moons, anchored by the heavy, submerged ring of a liquid-chilled vibraphone. High-velocity lap steel glissandos mutate into cosmic ray bursts, while weeping fiddles are fed through vacuum-tube pitch shifters to simulate planetary gravity-slingshots. The rhythm pulses with the irregular slosh of blackwater ballast tanks mixed with a hard-scrabble, train-beat shuffle, creating a disorienting sensation of floating endlessly upward while rooted in wet, red-clay dirt.

